Z||000004||Formula88||06-18-2001||09:30 PM||||The only real advantage to Platinum plugs is they last longer.  That's fine in a daily driver or if you plan on going 100K miles between tune ups.  In my Fiero, I want better performance.  It's gonna get tuned pretty regularly anyway, so the Platinum doesn't really give me a benifit.  But I've had good luck with AC plugs in many different cars.  Although I don't recommend their Platinum.  Too expensive for what you get.||||reg||1
Z||000005||p4n1c||06-18-2001||09:35 PM||||Actually, I've heard from a number of W-Body people that the Bosch platinum plugs don't last long in GM engines(at least the ones used in the W-Bodies(2.8, 3.1, 3.4, 3.8)).  The tips get burnt right off in a short number of miles because of the heat of the spark generated.<P>"<B>Recommendation NOT to use Bosch Platinum</B><BR>Bosch Platinum (and Platinum Plus 4) spark plugs use a center conductor which is a tiny platinum electrode that is totally recessed into a ceramic center conductor. After 10,000-15,000 miles, the center electrode may wear down. Apparently the spark generated by GM's ignition system is just too hot, and erodes the tiny center electrode away very quickly. I have been told that this may be a result of GM's waste-spark method of Distributorless Ignition System (where plugs are fired in pairs, one plug fires on the compression stroke while the other fires a wasted spark). At any rate, this has occured on almost every W-body car owner that has tried them. It is not unusual to find the tiny pinpoint center electrode worn well below the surface of the ceramic insulator to the point where the electrode can no longer be seen. The design is rather poor, because at this point, the plug cannot be reliably re-gapped."<P>This from  <A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/gm_w_body/upgrades/engine-sparkplugs.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/gm_w_body/upgrades/engine-sparkplugs.html</A>  .<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>1988 Olds Cutlass Supreme International<BR>2.8L MPFI V6/TH440-T4<BR>*Under Restoration*||||reg||1
